        "referenceRadiusMeters": 45500
      },
      "coverage": "Convex light-curve reconstruction with the thermally preferred pole and a published 90–92 km diameter fit range. The archive mesh uses 91 km; another pole remains possible. The grid marks unavailable imagery; rotational phase is illustrative. Delbo and Tanga2009 supplementary section on Lydia explicitly choose pole1 (149.3,-55), matching model152, because it fits slightly better (reduced chi-square0.7 versus0.76). The second pole remains possible. Its IRAS thermophysical diameter range is90–92 km versus94–97 km for pole2; the archive stores91±1 km.",
